========
Order by
========
select order_value from order order by order_value;

Order by guarantees total ordering as there is only 1 reducer is used.

there are some limitations in the "order by" clause.

In strict mode limit clause is compulsory

hive.mapred.mode=strict;

use strict mode so that it will make limit clause compulsory so that we dont put more burden while doing order by.

order of nulls will be shown first in asc ORDER

========
sort by
========

select order_value from order sort by order_value;

sort by can use multiple reducers.

local sorting happens on each reducer so we can't guarantee a total ordering

when there is only reducer, output of both sort by and order by will be same. 

below 2 properties define how many reducers will be there:

set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer

by default set to 250MB

this means if mappers are giving 1 GB data then 4 reducers will come into the pictures

set mapred.reduce.tasks

by dafault it is -1 (minus 1)

if it is -1 then by default it will consider other property which is 250 MB

so if we set set mapred.reduce.tasks=2 then 2 reducers will come into the picture.

